{"id": "EUVD-2026-101566", "enisaUuid": "3b2959c4-27ee-394f-9e1e-2a999124a253", "description": "Colanode server through 0.4.7 contains a path traversal vulnerability that allows authenticated users to read arbitrary .jpeg files by supplying an encoded traversal sequence in avatarId. Attackers can send percent-encoded ../ sequences to GET /client/v1/avatars/:avatarId to escape the avatars directory and read .jpeg files belonging to other workspaces.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T18:47:43", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T19:38:51", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@hieuPenguinnn/colanode-avatar-download-path-traversal", "https://github.com/colanode/colanode/blob/d649523637f0f059c936418488165d4a689da27c/apps/server/src/lib/storage/fs.ts#L38", "https://github.com/colanode/colanode/blob/d649523637f0f059c936418488165d4a689da27c/apps/server/src/api/client/routes/avatars/avatar-download.ts#L23", "https://github.com/colanode/colanode", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/colanode-server-through-0.4.7-path-traversal-via-avatar-download-route"], "aliases": ["GHSA-wq2v-xq4c-mvch", "CVE-2026-110766"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.29, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "cda9dd4e-b88b-310f-b4ae-8c3bcf3791a2", "product": {"name": "colanode", "vendor": {"name": "colanode"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.4.7"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "d8db81f7-4837-382e-9348-0720ff1715f2", "vendor": {"name": "colanode"}}], "isExploited": false}